<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emerald Buddha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Phra Kaeo Morakot</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Emerald Buddha is a small statue of the seated Buddha carved from green jade, the palladium of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. Kept for centuries in Lan Na, it was taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Prabang</a> and then Vientiane in the 16th century. Chao Phraya Chakri carried it off to Thonburi in 1779, and since 1784 it has stood in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wat-phra-kaew">Wat Phra Kaew</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emerald-buddha.jpg" alt="Emerald Buddha" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: กสิณธร ราชโอรส · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%A8%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%A8%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A1%E0%B9%81%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%9A%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%8A%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%87_%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%82%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%A3_%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%87%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%A3_(51).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
